WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.992
The LEGO company is famous for its small plastic bricks.

2
00:00:06.993 --> 00:00:10.237
They can be used to build just about anything!

3
00:00:10.238 --> 00:00:13.439
Kids build and play with LEGO sets.

4
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.884
Even many adults collect them.

5
00:00:16.885 --> 00:00:21.149
But LEGO didn't always make this popular construction toy.

6
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:29.934
In 1916 a woodworker named Ole Kirk Christiansen started a small business in Denmark.

7
00:00:29.935 --> 00:00:36.787
Ole's business made household items like ironing boards and ladders.

8
00:00:36.788 --> 00:00:40.795
By 1932 Ole's son Godtfred was working with him.

9
00:00:40.796 --> 00:00:44.393
Godtfred was 12 years old.

10
00:00:44.394 --> 00:00:48.633
Ole started making blocks and other wooden toys that year.

11
00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:53.839
These sold better than his ironing boards!

12
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.914
With the success of his toys, Ole stopped making household items.

13
00:00:58.915 --> 00:01:02.461
The company began making more toys.

14
00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:07.391
Some of them were made of plastic, like models of cars and trucks.

15
00:01:07.392 --> 00:01:09.740
This was very daring.

16
00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:13.937
Many people thought plastic toys would never be popular.

17
00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:19.027
Most toys in those days were made of wood or metal.

18
00:01:19.028 --> 00:01:21.810
Ole named his company LEGO.

19
00:01:21.811 --> 00:01:25.771
The name came from a Danish phrase that means "play well."

20
00:01:25.772 --> 00:01:28.630
But that's not the only meaning.

21
00:01:28.631 --> 00:01:34.982
Ole and Godtfred would later find out that LEGO means "I put together" in Latin.

22
00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:39.723
By the 1950s Godtfred was all grown up.

23
00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:43.773
He also had more responsibility at the company.

24
00:01:43.774 --> 00:01:48.254
One of his ideas was for interlocking building blocks.

25
00:01:48.255 --> 00:01:53.439
In 1958 he invented the now-famous LEGO brick design.

26
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.901
It's the same design in use today!

27
00:01:56.902 --> 00:02:03.274
The plastic bricks were so popular that LEGO stopped making wooden toys.

28
00:02:03.275 --> 00:02:07.244
Unfortunately Ole died that same year.

29
00:02:07.245 --> 00:02:09.889
So Godtfred took over the company.

30
00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.046
He helped it to grow.

31
00:02:12.047 --> 00:02:18.716
In 1969 LEGO created a series of larger bricks for young children.

32
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:23.776
In 1978 LEGO created their famous people figures.

33
00:02:23.777 --> 00:02:29.267
LEGO has made over four billion of these smiling yellow figures.

34
00:02:29.268 --> 00:02:34.226
LEGO also introduced themed sets like castles and spaceships.

35
00:02:34.227 --> 00:02:37.562
Pirate sets came out in 1989.

36
00:02:37.563 --> 00:02:41.516
And more themed sets have been created since then.

37
00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:44.671
Over the years, the LEGO company has grown a lot.

38
00:02:44.672 --> 00:02:50.222
Besides LEGO toys, there are movies, books, and theme parks.

39
00:02:50.223 --> 00:02:58.488
LEGO bricks are tiny toys—but they sure are hugely popular!

